  "name": "@ingenx-io/valets-schema-mcp-server",
  "readme": "# @ingenx-io/valets-schema-mcp-server\n\nMCP server that exposes the [Valets](https://github.com/IngenX-IO/valets-data-architecture) data model documentation to AI agents via the [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io).\n\n## Usage\n\n### Claude Desktop\n\nAdd to `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"valets-schema\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@ingenx-io/valets-schema-mcp-server\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Claude Code\n\n```bash\nclaude mcp add valets-schema -- npx -y @ingenx-io/valets-schema-mcp-server\n```\n\n### Other MCP clients\n\n```json\n{\n  \"command\": \"npx\",\n  \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@ingenx-io/valets-schema-mcp-server\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Remote (Claude custom connector)\n\nThe server ships two transports from the same tool/resource definitions\n(`create-server.js`):\n\n| Entrypoint | Transport | Use |\n|------------|-----------|-----|\n| `index.js` (`npm start`) | stdio | Local / npx, Claude Desktop, Claude Code |\n| `http.js` (`npm run start:http`) | Streamable HTTP | Remote deployment / Claude custom connector |\n\nTo expose it as a custom connector:\n\n1. **Bundle the data** (snapshots `schema-docs` outputs *and* the canonical Zod\n   schemas into `data/`). `bundle.js` hard-fails if the Zod bundle is missing, so\n   build it first \u2014 or just run `make generate` from the repo root, which does both:\n   ```bash\n   pnpm --dir ../schema-package build:standalone   # \u2192 data/schema/valets-schema.mjs\n   npm run bundle\n   ```\n2. **Build & run the HTTP transport** (binds to `$PORT`, default 3000):\n   ```bash\n   docker build -t valets-schema-mcp .\n   docker run -p 8080:8080 valets-schema-mcp\n   # or, without Docker:\n   PORT=8080 npm run start:http\n   ```\n3. **Deploy** to any always-on Node host behind a public HTTPS URL. The\n   process must stay running \u2014 a static docs host is not sufficient.\n   Health check: `GET /health`.\n   - **Recommended: Dokku** \u2014 git-push deploy reusing existing infra, with\n     the build bundling `data/` itself (no host prep). See\n     [`DEPLOY-DOKKU.md`](./DEPLOY-DOKKU.md). The Dokku build uses\n     `Dockerfile.mcp` at the repo root.\n   - Other hosts (Cloud Run, Fly.io, Railway, Render\u2026) work too \u2014 build the\n     repo-root `Dockerfile.mcp` (multi-arch; includes the docs site).\n4. **Add the connector** in Claude \u2192 Settings \u2192 Connectors \u2192 *Add custom\n   connector* \u2192 point it at `https://<your-host>/mcp`.\n\nThe remote (`http.js`) build also serves the Docusaurus docs site at `/` (baked\ninto the image, multi-stage build), so one URL serves both: `/` for humans,\n`/mcp` for agents.\n\nThe endpoint is **stateless** (a fresh server instance per request), so it\nscales horizontally with no sticky sessions.\n\n> \u26a0\ufe0f **No authentication yet.** The remote endpoint is currently\n> unauthenticated and serves read-only public schema docs. OAuth\n> resource-server support is tracked separately \u2014 do not expose anything\n> private until that lands.\n\n## Tools\n\n| Tool | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `schema_overview` | High-level summary of all models and enums \u2014 start here |\n| `get_schema` | JSON Schema for a specific model or enum (kebab-case, e.g. `order`, `payment-status`) |\n| `get_doc` | Raw Markdown documentation for a schema page (e.g. `models/order`, `enums/payment-method`) |\n| `search_docs` | Keyword search across all documentation pages |\n| `list_decisions` | All data model decisions (D00\u2013D37+) with status and summary |\n| `get_decision` | Full details for a specific decision by ID (e.g. `D12`) |\n| `get_openapi` | OpenAPI 3.1 spec \u2014 full or filtered to a single component (e.g. `Order`, `OrderCreate`) |\n| `get_guidance` | Use-case recipes: tool call sequences, field constraint cheatsheets, and workaround notes. Call with no args for the index, or pass a `slug` for the full recipe. |\n| `validate_document` | Validate a document against the **canonical Zod schema** \u2014 cross-field `.refine()` rules included. Returns `{ valid, errors: [{ path, message, code }] }`. |\n| `snapshot_info` | Provenance + freshness of the data being served: `generated` timestamp, age in days, package version, and a `stale` flag. Call it to **verify you are reasoning against a current contract**. |\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f This server serves a point-in-time SNAPSHOT\n\nThe schema data ships **inside the npm package** (`data/static/\u2026`). It is a snapshot, not a live feed.\n\n**`npx -y` reuses its cached install** rather than re-resolving against npm on each launch, so a client can keep running an obsolete contract **indefinitely, and silently**. This is not hypothetical: during a conformance audit ([ING-658](https://github.com/IngenX-IO/valets-data-architecture/issues/174)) a cached server faithfully reported **D65 / 49 models** while upstream was already at **D76 / 63** \u2014 and the audit twice concluded \"nothing changed.\"\n\nThe server was not lying. There was simply no signal that the snapshot was old. Now there is:\n\n- `schema_overview` prints the snapshot's `generated` timestamp and age in its header.\n- After **14 days** (override with `VALETS_STALE_AFTER_DAYS`) it prints a loud staleness warning.\n- `snapshot_info` returns the same facts **machine-readably**, so an agent can assert on freshness without parsing prose.\n\n**To force a refresh:** `npx -y @ingenx-io/valets-schema-mcp-server@latest` (or clear the npx cache).\n\n**To bypass the bundle entirely:** set `VALETS_SCHEMA_URL` to a deployed instance \u2014 data is then fetched live and staleness does not apply.\n\n## `validate_document` (D72 / [#163](https://github.com/IngenX-IO/valets-data-architecture/issues/163))\n\n```\nvalidate_document(model=\"stock-movement\", document={ \u2026, \"quantity\": 0 })\n\u2192 {\n    \"model\": \"stock-movement\",\n    \"variant\": \"read\",\n    \"valid\": false,\n    \"errors\": [\n      { \"path\": \"quantity\",\n        \"message\": \"quantity must be non-zero (D76): a movement of zero moves nothing\u2026\",\n        \"code\": \"custom\" }\n    ]\n  }\n```\n\n**This is an oracle, not a shape check.** It runs the same Zod schemas the backend runs,\nloaded from a vendored build of `@ingenx-io/valets-schema`. Validating against the published\nJSON Schema instead would be a rubber stamp: `z.toJSONSchema()` **drops every `.refine()`**\n([#170](https://github.com/IngenX-IO/valets-data-architecture/issues/170)), so an\najv-over-JSON-Schema validator cannot see D76's signed-quantity rule, the WhatsApp\n`kind`\u21c4payload exclusivity, the `price`/`priceDelta` XOR, and ten more. An error with\n`\"code\": \"custom\"` **is** one of those cross-field rules firing.\n\nThe schemas are **vendored, not npm-installed** (`data/schema/valets-schema.mjs`, produced by\n`npm run bundle`): `@ingenx-io/valets-schema` publishes to GitHub Packages (auth-gated) while\nthis package publishes to public npm, so a dependency on it would make `npx` 404 for everyone.\n`zod` is already a dependency here (the MCP SDK needs it), so the vendored bundle adds bytes\nand no new dependency.\n\n### Variants: `read` only, on purpose\n\n| Variant | Status |\n|---------|--------|\n| `read` (default) | \u2705 Supported \u2014 validates a **stored** document (the full shape, server-set fields present). |\n| `create` / `update` | \u274c Explicit not-supported error, with a pointer to `get_openapi(\"<Model>Create\"/\"<Model>Update\")`. |\n\nThe Zod source **is** the read shape. A write projection would need the server-set fields made\noptional *while keeping the refines* \u2014 and Zod 4 refuses: `.partial()` throws on an object\nschema carrying refinements. The only ways through are to drop the refines (reinstating exactly\nthe rubber stamp this tool exists to kill) or to run whole-document rules against a partial\npayload (which invents failures \u2014 `price`-XOR-`priceDelta` \"fails\" on an update touching\nneither). A half-working verdict is worse than none, so `create`/`update` fail loudly instead.\nWiring them properly means materialising the D72 projections in the Zod source, not here.\n\n## Cookbook\n\n`get_guidance` exposes a set of use-case recipes \u2014 each one describes the right sequence of MCP tool calls for a specific task.\n\n### Available recipes\n\n| Slug | When to use |\n|------|-------------|\n| `write-model-code` | You need to read or write a Firestore document and want to know which fields are server-set, immutable, or deprecated. |\n| `field-history` | You found a field and want to understand why it exists, what decision drove it, and whether it's been migrated. |\n| `whatsapp-conversation-display` | You need to render a per-order WhatsApp message thread. Uses `NotificationRecord` as a workaround (outbound only). |\n\n### Example usage\n\n```\n# Get the index\nget_guidance()\n\n# Get a specific recipe\nget_guidance(slug=\"write-model-code\")\nget_guidance(slug=\"whatsapp-conversation-display\")\n```\n\nEach recipe returns JSON with ordered `steps` (tool + args + note), tips, and any relevant caveats or cheatsheets.\n\n## Resources\n\n| URI | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| `valets://schemas.json` | Consolidated JSON Schema bundle for all models and enums |\n| `valets://llms.txt` | LLM-optimized summary of the Valets data model |\n| `valets://openapi.yaml` | OpenAPI 3.1 specification |\n| `valets://decisions.json` | Data model decisions metadata |\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `VALETS_SCHEMA_URL` | _(unset)_ | Base URL of a deployed Valets Docusaurus site. When set, the server fetches live data from this URL and falls back to bundled data on failure. |\n| `VALETS_CACHE_TTL` | `300000` | Cache TTL in milliseconds for remotely fetched data (default: 5 minutes). |\n\nWhen `VALETS_SCHEMA_URL` is not set, the server uses the bundled schema snapshot included in the package.\n",
  "readmeFilename": "README.md",
